From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: compare the polygon vertex normal with inexact_equal

test-py-polygonal-surface.py's test_polygon_vertex_normal checks the
vertex normal at vertex 0 (shared by two triangles meeting there) with
an exact `!=` against the literal (0, 0, 1). The computed normal goes
through a cross product, an accumulation across the two adjacent
triangles and a normalize() (sqrt-based) - it only lands exactly on
(0, 0, 1) when every multiply-add in that chain is rounded separately.

Same root cause as the existing 0001 patch in this directory (GCC's
default -ffp-contract=fast fuses multiply-adds into FMA on riscv64's
rv64gc baseline, one ULP away from the literal answer; upstream only
ships baseline x86_64/win_amd64 wheels, neither of which contracts, so
this has never run on an FMA target). Same fix: switch to inexact_equal
(GLOBAL_EPSILON = 1e-6), which other tests in this same file and
elsewhere in the suite already use for computed results. Vector3D
inherits inexact_equal from Point3D's pybind11 binding (vector.cpp
registers class_<Vector3D, Point3D>); no new binding needed. The
library code is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against Geode-solutions/OpenGeode]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 bindings/python/tests/mesh/test-py-polygonal-surface.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bindings/python/tests/mesh/test-py-polygonal-surface.py b/bindings/python/tests/mesh/test-py-polygonal-surface.py
index f6d2504..e5d1a0c 100644
--- a/bindings/python/tests/mesh/test-py-polygonal-surface.py
+++ b/bindings/python/tests/mesh/test-py-polygonal-surface.py
@@ -209,7 +209,7 @@ def test_polygon_vertex_normal():
     builder.compute_polygon_adjacencies()

     answer = geom.Vector3D([0., 0., 1.])
-    if polygonal_surface.polygon_vertex_normal(0) != answer:
+    if not polygonal_surface.polygon_vertex_normal(0).inexact_equal(answer):
         raise ValueError(
             "[Test] PolygonalSurface polygon vertex normal is not correct")

